      "description": "Sul Ross State University Applicant Portal | Dual Credit Lecturer or Adjunct Instructor of Biology Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help HR Home Page Dual Credit Lecturer or Adjunct Instructor of Biology Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. PLEASE NOTE : All applications should contain complete job history entries, which includes job title, dates of employment, name of employer, supervisor’s name and phone number and a description of duties performed. If this information is not submitted, your application may be rejected because it is incomplete. Resumes and curriculum vitae do not take the place of this required information. Posting Details Posting Details Instructions to applicants PLEASE NOTE : All applications should contain complete job history entries, which includes job title, dates of employment, name of employer, supervisor’s name and phone number and a description of duties performed. If this information is not submitted, your application may be rejected because it is incomplete. Resumes and curriculum vitae do not take the place of this required information. Job Title Dual Credit Lecturer or Adjunct Instructor of Biology Location Del Rio, Uvalde or Eagle Pass Department Natural Sciences Job No. AJF983 Posting Date 08/17/2026 End Date 08/31/2027 Until Filled No Appointment Date 09/01/2026 Salary $2,550-$3,200/class as determined by qualifications and enrollments Required Master’s degree in Biology or a related field from an accredited institution. Classroom teaching experience. Preferred Ph. D. in Biology from an accredited institution and prior university teaching experience. Blackboard experience. Primary Responsibilities Primary Responsibilities: The Natural & Behavioral Sciences Department periodically seeks qualified, part-time instructors to teach freshman and sophomore-level biology courses. Teach face 