      "title": "Dual Credit Lecturer or Adjunct Instructor in Sociology 2026-2027",
      "description": "Sul Ross State University Applicant Portal | Dual Credit Lecturer or Adjunct Instructor in Sociology 2026-2027 Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help HR Home Page Dual Credit Lecturer or Adjunct Instructor in Sociology 2026-2027 Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. PLEASE NOTE: All applications should contain complete job history entries, which includes job title, dates of employment, name of employer, supervisor’s name and phone number and a description of duties performed. If this information is not submitted, your application may be rejected because it is incomplete. Resumes and curriculum vitae do not take the place of this required information. Posting Details Posting Details Instructions to applicants PLEASE NOTE : All applications should contain complete job history entries, which includes job title, dates of employment, name of employer, supervisor’s name and phone number and a description of duties performed. If this information is not submitted, your application may be rejected because it is incomplete. Resumes and curriculum vitae do not take the place of this required information. Job Title Dual Credit Lecturer or Adjunct Instructor in Sociology 2026-2027 Location Alpine Department Provost VPASA Academics Job No. AFJ982 Posting Date 07/24/2026 End Date Until Filled Yes Appointment Date Salary $2,700 per 3-SCH course Required Master’s degree in Sociology or a master’s degree with 18 graduate hours in Sociology. Classroom teaching experience. Preferred PHD and prior University teaching experience. Blackboard experience. Primary Responsibilities SRSU seeks qualified, adjunct/part-time instructors to teach dual credit students enrolled in freshman- and sophomore-level university courses in Sociology . • Teach online, synchronous courses at a variety of days and times • Create engaging lessons that promote student