      "title": "Noyce Graduate Research Assistant 2026-2027",
      "description": "Sul Ross State University Applicant Portal | Noyce Graduate Research Assistant 2026-2027 Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help HR Home Page Noyce Graduate Research Assistant 2026-2027 Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. PLEASE NOTE : All applications should contain complete job history entries, which includes job title, dates of employment, name of employer, supervisor’s name and phone number and a description of duties performed. If this information is not submitted, your application may be rejected because it is incomplete. Resumes and curriculum vitae do not take the place of this required information. Posting Details Posting Details Instructions to applicants PLEASE NOTE : All applications should contain complete job history entries, which includes job title, dates of employment, name of employer, supervisor’s name and phone number and a description of duties performed. If this information is not submitted, your application may be rejected because it is incomplete. Resumes and curriculum vitae do not take the place of this required information. Job Title Noyce Graduate Research Assistant 2026-2027 Location Alpine Department College of Education Job No. 999068 Posting Date 07/30/2026 End Date 05/02/2027 Until Filled Yes Appointment Date 09/01/2026 Salary $1,000 - $1,250 monthly based on completed credit hours Required Bachelor’s degree, enrollment in a minimum of 6 hrs graduate course work per semester. Strong technical. writing, and digital literacy skills. Preferred M.Ed Graduate Student. Primary Responsibilities The Noyce Graduate Research Assistant will the support recruiting, retention, program coordination and evaluation of the Robert Noyce NSF grant program. Duties include: Recruitment Support Assist in coordinating and supporting outreach activities to inform eligible candidates about scholarship opportunities and program requirements. Distribute informational materials through approved university and community channels. Track and report recruitment metrics and engagement outcomes. Program Coordination Provide logistical support for program events, workshops, and seminars. Assist in scheduling meetings, managing communication with participants, and documenting event outcomes. Help maintain an organized digital archive of program resources and materials. Research Assistance Collect, organize, and code qualitative and quantitative data related to program activities and outcomes. Conduct literature reviews relevant to STEM teacher preparation, retention, and related fields. Support preparation of academic posters, presentations, and publications for dissemination efforts. Data Management and Analysis Input and manage data using appropriate software (e.g., Excel, SPSS , Media). Assist with analyzing trends and patterns for reporting to NSF and institutional stakeholders. Security Sensitive: This position is classified as Security-Sensitive and is thereby subject to the provisions of Texas Education Code §51.215 and Texas Government Code §411.094, which authorize employers to obtain and review criminal history record information for applicants. Responsible for personal safety and the safety of others; must exercise due caution and practice safe work habits at all times. Other Information An Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer It is the policy of Sul Ross State University to provide equal employment opportunity for all persons in accordance with their individual, job related qualifications and without consideration of race, creed, color, sex, religion, age, national origin, disability, sexual orientation, gender identity, veteran status and ancestry. Equal employment opportunities shall be afforded in all personnel actions or decisions including, but not necessarily limited to, recruitment, hiring, training, upgrading, promotion, demotion, termination and salary. R